      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in GCA (tocilizumab):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " IL-6 receptor antagonist; consider when starting corticosteroids: allows an accelerated steroid taper and ↓steroid exposure; higher rates of sustained remission once steroids stop; optimal duration ⍉determined; caution w Hx of diverticulitis (diverticular perf)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) dose, giant cell arteritis (GCA):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " IV 6 mg per kg Q4wks w tapering course of glucocorticoids. SC: 162 mg Q1wk w tapering course of glucocorticoids; 162 mg once every other wk may be prescribed based on clin considerations."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑ risk of serious infect that may lead to hsp or death; most pts were taking concomitant immunosuppressants such as MTX or corticosteroids. Test for latent TB b4 ACTEMRA use and during therapy (except pts w COVID-19); start tx for latent infect prior to ACTEMRA use."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " known hypersensitivity to ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
